<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105815" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρωπάω</span></b> , poet. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρέπω,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>turn, change,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥ τε θαμὰ τρωπῶσα χέει πολυηχέα
			φωνήν,</span> of the nightingale, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.521
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, <i>turn oneself, turn about,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάλιν τρωπᾶσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.95
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς πόλιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					24.536
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόβονδε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.666
				</span></i>
			; 
				Ep.
			 Iterat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρωπάσκετο φεύγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.568
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρωπασκέσθω: μεταβαλλέσθω,
				ἐπιστρεφέσθω,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
